{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Samuel is dead and buried [B]in Ramah
All Israel mourned his [D#m]passing away
Saul had driven mediums out [B]of the land
But fear now gripped [D#m]his trembling heart
Philistines camped at [B]Shunem in sight
Israel waited at Gilboa that night
He inquired of the LORD for [B]a sign
But no answer came [D#m]through dream or [B]line
Not by U[C#]rim nor by prophets' [B]call
Silence held [C#]him in [A#sus4]the [A#]empty [D#m]hall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why have you dis[F#]turbed me by bringing me up
[C#]The LORD has turned away and [B]become your en[D#m]emy
He has torn the [F#]kingdom out of your hand
And given [C#]it to David your neighbor to[B]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D#m]Saul disguised himself in other clothes
Took two [B]men to the woman at [D#m]night
Asked her to consult a spirit for him
She [B]asked who he would want to [D#m]find
Bring up Samuel he whispered low
She [B]cried out in a sudden [D#m]flow
Why have you deceived me she exclaimed
I [B]see you clearly you are [D#m]Saul
[B]An old man wrapped [C#]in a robe is com[D#m]ing
Rising up from the ground so lonely
[B]Saul bowed his face to [C#]the dusty ground
[A#]Trembling before the prophet found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Why have you disturbed me by [F#]bringing me up
The LORD has [C#]turned away and become your [B]enemy
[D#m]He has torn the kingdom [F#]out of your hand
And given it to [C#]David your neighbor to[B]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Because you did not o[C#]bey the voice of the [D#m]LORD
And [B]failed his burning an[C#]ger against Ama[D#m]lek
The [B]LORD will hand both [C#]you and Israel o[D#m]ver
To the [B]Philistines [C#]in the [D#m]dark
To[B]morrow you and your [C#]sons will be with [D#m]me
And the [B]army will fall in de[A#]feat
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D#m]Saul fell full length on the [F#]ground in fear
His [C#]strength was gone and his [B]spirit broke
They [D#m]ate and left in the dark [F#]of the night
With no hope [C#]left in the [B]sight
{end_of_verse}

